#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105679 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a4270f2-daf1-532d-804a-f293b6f1a8be" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Polygon"}] :question/id #uuid "36445a36-7b68-5ba1-847e-7fd720138dd6" :question/math-academy-id "e-7859" :question/problem "The stretch $S(x,y) = \\left(\\dfrac{3}{2}x,2y\\right)$ is applied to the polygon shown below. Find the resulting polygon.\n\n![](images/a3/a36f0ee4e491e0518041f7e033392b9f16e12c4e2501e707d8328af78aa89efd.png)" :question/worked-solution "To stretch a polygon, we\n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(2,1)$, $(4,1)$, $(2,2)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(2, 1) & ↦ (\\frac{3}{2} \\cdot 2, 2 \\cdot 1) = (3, 2) \\\\ (4, 1) & ↦ (\\frac{3}{2} \\cdot 4, 2 \\cdot 1) = (6, 2) \\\\ (2, 2) & ↦ (\\frac{3}{2} \\cdot 2, 2 \\cdot 2) = (3, 4)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/b9/b961a446536bddbe6ff529e7ca2973c8e957c185ef4d6f00b9255d09baa9d3cc.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105680 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "043fb5ef-143e-53cc-b83a-15df50446af4" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Combined Stretches Using Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "228d023c-b74d-56a9-ab02-638594472f43" :question/math-academy-id "e-7860" :question/problem "What function represents the combined stretch of factor $4$ in the $x$-direction and factor $\\dfrac 1 4$ in the $y$-direction?" :question/worked-solution "- A stretch in the $x$-direction of factor $4$ can be represented by the function\n$(x,y)\\mapsto (4x,y)$.\n- A stretch in the $y$-direction of factor $\\dfrac 1 4$ can be represented by the function\n$(x,y)\\mapsto \\left(x,\\dfrac 1 4y\\right)$.\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto \\left(4x,\\dfrac 1 4y\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105681 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28d37803-32d2-5b80-aa78-2f0d728e18fe" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "50e74298-c5c0-5bda-bb64-18778f156508" :question/math-academy-id "e-7861" :question/problem "The point $(2,5)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2$, and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $-2$. What is the resulting point?" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n$(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(2x,y\\right)$.\n- A stretch of factor $-2$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n$(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(x,-2y\\right)$.\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left({\\color{blue}2}x,{\\color{red}-2}y\\right)\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(2,5) \\mapsto \\left(2\\cdot 2, \\, -2\\cdot5 \\right) = (4,-10)\n$$\n\n![](images/0d/0d050ec1579f2ea2b37c01f2d7b60fd6580b6bc4766fcdd66005e1c2c103b8c7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106534 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28d37803-32d2-5b80-aa78-2f0d728e18fe" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae5059f-bcf0-56ad-8d2b-a7753f3f2165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105353} {:answer/id #uuid "b201a497-ee1e-576e-bbfc-e07b6cd6db5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8, 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105354} {:answer/id #uuid "d7670310-6908-57ff-a1cc-003fdf97fe7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105355} {:answer/id #uuid "f14e16fb-3741-5173-a681-76727ba988b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4, 12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105356} {:answer/id #uuid "7210917c-c758-5039-9de4-dd42047b5fa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8, 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105357}] :answer-field/id #uuid "af8b2139-6d53-5b18-926c-04ee1c2734e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105352}] :question/id #uuid "20947e98-c606-5c7e-861f-e50700e68b13" :question/math-academy-id "q-88617" :question/problem "The point $(4, 2)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2$, and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $-3$. What is the resulting point?"}]}
